    "blurb": "Respond to external Nextcloud requests",
    "overview": "The Nextcloud Inbound connector responds to external requests from Nextcloud and passes their metadata directly to Camunda BPMN processes. Start new process instances or trigger actions in running ones when files and folders are created, updated, or deleted.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Respond to external requests from Nextcloud",
    "splashDescription": "The Nextcloud Inbound connector for Camunda is a custom connector that enables event-driven integration between Nextcloud and Camunda process orchestration. By leveraging Nextcloud’s Webhook Listeners app, events such as file creations, updates, deletions, or folder changes can be captured in real time and forwarded to Camunda as structured event data. These events can be used to start new process instances or trigger actions within running processes. The connector ensures that all relevant metadata (e.g. file properties, user actions, timestamps) is directly available within your BPMN process models, enabling seamless integration of document-centric events into end-to-end business processes. This allows organizations to react immediately to changes in their document landscape, orchestrate document-driven processes (e.g. routing, approval, archiving, synchronization), implement centralized governance and decision logic for incoming events, and connect file-based operations with broader automation initiatives across BPM, RPA, low-code, and AI-based services. In addition, a central control layer can be implemented to define which events are processed and how they are handled, ensuring consistency, compliance, and flexibility in document-driven automation scenarios. Disclaimer: Nextcloud is a trademark of Nextcloud GmbH. This connector is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nextcloud.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/873771/overview/img17771183565391411736.png?45a8e4106f671c79b5a57ed2355dabf7",
